timestamp=2026-11-05T12:55:29.673Z level=INFO run=3351243d message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So maintenance windows that count (exclude readings during them): \n# - \"System firmware update on Sakura Energy Site on the 16th of March from 08:00 to 12:00 local time. Status: COMPLETED.\"\n# - \"Panel inspection on Sakura Energy Site on March 15th from 09:00 to 11:00 local time. CANCELLED due to heavy rain.\" -> CANCELLED, so NOT successfully conducted? \"Readings recorded during successfully conducted maintenance windows must be excluded from the analysis.\" So only if COMPLETED/successfully conducted - CANCELLED means do NOT exclude.\n# - \"Scheduled cleaning at Vistula Photovoltaics on March 15, starting at 12:00 and finishing at 14:00 local time. Status: COMPLETED.\"\n\n# Also the safety rule: \"If inverter_temperature_C exceeds 85.0C, the unit enters emergency shutdown. Readings for the 45 minutes immediately following such a spike must be invalidated.\"\n# That affects all farms? It's a general safety rule. We need to track when temp > 85.0 and then invalidate readings for next 45 minutes from that spike event? The phrasing: \"Readings for the 45 minutes immediately following such a spike must be invalidated.\" So any reading timestamp that falls within that 45-minute window after a spike is invalidated.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
