timestamp=2026-11-05T13:50:01.377Z level=INFO run=3351243d message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Check FARM_T - huge value 1.78e9. FARM_T is energy, unit MWh, calib offset 0.05, value col mwh_yield. So if readings are in MWh, we multiply by 1000 to get kWh. Also offset is 0.05 in same units (MWh)? The calibration offset is applied to the recorded value as stated - probably in the same units as the recorded value. So if value is in MWh, offset 0.05 means 0.05 MWh. Then true = recorded - offset (MWh); and then convert to kWh by multiplying by 1000. That means the offset contributes 0.05*1000=50 kWh per reading? That’s correct as a constant shift. But could the magnitude be right? Let us look at FARM_T data.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
